42:**Band (sheet 8).** A6: the split of lines between the two tails is the table `BAND_SPLIT` at the top of `make_netlist.py` (section 11, change e). J_BAND_A (joystick side, 8 pads): 1 UP (JOY_UP), 2 DOWN (JOY_DOWN), 3 LEFT (JOY_LEFT), 4 RIGHT (JOY_RIGHT), 5 CENTRE (BTN_REC), 6 MOT- (GND, A7 W2), 7 MOT+ (VMOT, A7 W1), 8 GND (GND). J_BAND_B (other tail, 7 pads): 1 CELL+ (VBAT), 2 CELL- (GND), 3 NTC (NTC), 4 VBUS (VBUS), 5 D- (USB_DN), 6 D+ (USB_DP), 7 GND (GND). Behind them: SW1 up, SW3 down, SW4 LEFT (toward the hand), SW5 RIGHT (toward the fingertip), each one SKTAAAE010 with terminal P1 on its line and P2 on ground; SW2 on BTN_REC is the switch under the centre of the round joystick cap CAP1 (architecture 17.11, 17.29; a long press of 1.0 s starts and stops a recording; there is no record button); M1 W0525AB001D (A7), + (red lead) on VMOT, - (blue lead) on ground; BT1 the curved cell, + on VBAT, - on ground; RT1 10 kohm NTC from NTC to ground, in the band at the cell; CP1 to CP4 the charging pads, VBUS, D-, D+, GND in order from -Y to +Y, on the inside face of the band (architecture 17.12). The pad order and pad numbers of the two tails are this schematic's own definition (not a maker pin).
